t is equivalent to $A \\land (C \\lor B)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(A \\land C) \\lor (A \\land B)$","choice2":"$(A \\lor C) \\land (A \\lor B)$","choice3":"$A \\lor (B \\land C)$","choice4":"$(A \\land C) \\land (A \\land B)$","choice5":"$(A \\lor C) \\lor (A \\lor B)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We distribute the conjunction over the disjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\nA \\land (C \\lor B) \\equiv (A \\land C) \\lor (A \\land B)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7077,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Conjunction"},"group":{"id":15102,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308675,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:13:19.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13425},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308685,"created":"2026-10-15T23:13:36.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13381,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:13 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":81055,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7077,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(P \\lor Q) \\land R?$</p>\n","choice1":" $(P \\land R) \\lor (R \\land Q)$","choice2":" $(R \\lor P) \\land (Q \\lor R)$","choice3":" $P \\lor (Q \\land R)$","choice4":" $P \\land (R \\lor Q)$","choice5":"  $(P \\land R) \\land (Q \\land R)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We distribute the conjunction over the disjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(P \\lor Q) \\land R \\equiv (P \\land R) \\lor (Q \\land R)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, since $Q \\land R \\equiv R \\land Q,$ we can write</p>\n<p>\\[\n(P \\land R) \\lor (Q \\land R) \\equiv (P \\land R) \\lor (R \\land Q).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7077,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Conjunction"},"group":{"id":15102,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308685,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:13:36.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13381},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308689,"created":"2026-10-15T23:13:54.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13781,"number":4,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:13 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":128635,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7077,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(\\neg P \\lor Q) \\land \\neg R?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(\\neg P \\land \\neg R) \\lor (Q \\land \\neg R)$","choice2":"$(\\neg P \\land Q) \\lor \\neg R$","choice3":"$(\\neg P \\land \\neg R) \\land (Q \\land \\neg R)$","choice4":"$\\neg P \\lor (Q \\land \\neg R)$ ","choice5":"$(\\neg P \\lor   \\neg R) \\lor (Q \\lor \\neg R)$ ","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We distribute the conjunction over the disjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(\\neg P \\lor Q) \\land \\neg R \\equiv (\\neg P \\land \\neg R) \\lor (Q \\land \\neg R)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7077,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Conjunction"},"group":{"id":15102,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308689,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:13:54.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13781},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308702,"created":"2026-10-15T23:14:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":16642,"number":5,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:14 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:17","question":{"id":81599,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7077,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $P \\land (Q \\lor R)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$ (Q \\land P) \\lor (R \\land P)$","choice2":"$R \\land (P \\lor Q)$","choice3":"$ (Q \\land P) \\land (R \\land P)$","choice4":"$P \\lor (Q \\land R)$","choice5":"$(R \\land Q) \\lor (R \\land P)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We distribute the conjunction over the disjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\nP \\land (Q \\lor R) \\equiv (P \\land Q) \\lor (P \\land R)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, since $P \\land Q \\equiv Q \\land P$ and $P \\land R \\equiv R \\land P,$ we can write</p>\n<p>\\[\n(P \\land Q) \\lor (P \\land R) \\equiv (Q \\land P) \\lor (R \\land P).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7077,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Conjunction"},"group":{"id":15102,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308702,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:14:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":16642},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":7124,"number":2,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction","answers":[{"id":62308716,"created":"2026-10-15T23:14:39.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14568,"number":6,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:14 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":81609,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7124,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(R \\land P) \\lor Q?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(Q \\lor R) \\land (P \\lor Q)$","choice2":"$(Q \\lor R) \\land P$","choice3":"$(Q \\lor R) \\lor (P \\land Q)$","choice4":"$(Q \\land R) \\land (P \\lor Q)$","choice5":"$R \\land (P \\lor Q)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(R \\land P) \\lor Q \\equiv (R \\lor Q) \\land (P \\lor Q)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, since $R \\lor Q \\equiv Q \\lor R,$ we can write\n\\[\n(R \\lor Q) \\land (P \\lor Q) \\equiv (Q \\lor R) \\land (P \\lor Q).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7124,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction"},"group":{"id":15104,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308716,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:14:39.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14568},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308724,"created":"2026-10-15T23:14:56.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13247,"number":7,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:14 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":81604,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7124,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(A \\land  B) \\lor C?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(A \\lor C) \\land (B \\lor C)$","choice2":"$(A \\land C) \\lor (B \\land C)$","choice3":"$A \\land (B \\lor C)$","choice4":"$A \\lor (B \\land C)$","choice5":"$(A \\lor C) \\lor (B \\lor C)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(A \\land  B) \\lor C \\equiv (A \\lor C) \\land (B \\lor C)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7124,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction"},"group":{"id":15104,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308724,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:14:56.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13247},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308731,"created":"2026-10-15T23:15:17.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":17296,"number":8,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:15 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:17","question":{"id":128626,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7124,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(A \\land B) \\lor \\neg C?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(A \\lor \\neg C) \\land (B \\lor \\neg C)$","choice2":"$A \\land (B \\lor \\neg C)$","choice3":"$(A  \\land  \\neg C)  \\lor (B  \\land  \\neg C)$","choice4":"$(A \\lor \\neg C) \\lor  (B \\lor \\neg C)$","choice5":"$(A  \\land \\neg C)    \\land (B  \\land \\neg C)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:\n\\[\n(A \\land B) \\lor \\neg C \\equiv (A \\lor \\neg C) \\land (B \\lor \\neg C)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7124,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction"},"group":{"id":15104,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308731,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:15:17.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":17296},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308742,"created":"2026-10-15T23:15:46.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":25415,"number":9,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:15 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:25","question":{"id":128640,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7124,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(R \\land P) \\lor \\neg Q?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(\\neg Q \\lor R) \\land (P \\lor \\neg Q)$","choice2":"$(\\neg Q \\lor R) \\land P$","choice3":"$(\\neg Q \\lor R) \\lor (P \\land \\neg Q)$","choice4":"$(\\neg Q \\land R) \\land (P \\lor \\neg Q)$","choice5":"$R \\land (P \\lor \\neg Q)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(R \\land P) \\lor \\neg Q \\equiv (R \\lor \\neg Q) \\land (P \\lor \\neg Q)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, since $R \\lor \\neg Q \\equiv \\neg Q \\lor R,$ we can write\n\\[\n(R \\lor \\neg Q) \\land (P \\lor \\neg Q) \\equiv (\\neg Q \\lor R) \\land (P \\lor \\neg Q).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7124,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction"},"group":{"id":15104,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308742,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:15:46.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":25415},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308779,"created":"2026-10-15T23:16:24.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":27083,"number":10,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:16 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:27","question":{"id":81610,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7124,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(\\neg P \\land Q) \\lor R?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(R \\lor \\neg P) \\land (R \\lor Q)$","choice2":"$(R \\lor P) \\land (\\neg Q \\lor R)$","choice3":"$(R \\lor \\neg P) \\lor (R \\lor P)$","choice4":"$(R \\lor \\neg P) \\land Q$","choice5":"$\\neg P \\land (R \\lor Q)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(\\neg P \\land Q) \\lor R \\equiv (\\neg P \\lor R) \\land (Q \\lor R)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, since $\\neg P \\lor R \\equiv R \\lor \\neg P$ and $Q \\lor R \\equiv R \\lor Q$ we can write\n\\[\n(\\neg P \\lor R) \\land (Q \\lor R) \\equiv (R \\lor \\neg P) \\land (R \\lor Q).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7124,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction"},"group":{"id":15104,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308779,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:16:24.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":27083},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":7078,"number":3,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions","answers":[{"id":62308789,"created":"2026-10-15T23:16:51.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14796,"number":11,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:16 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":81616,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7078,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(X \\land Y) \\lor (X \\land \\neg Z)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(Y \\lor \\neg Z) \\land X$","choice2":"$(Y \\lor \\neg Z) \\lor X$","choice3":"$X \\land (Y \\lor Z)$","choice4":"$X \\land (\\neg Y \\lor Z)$","choice5":"$(Y \\land \\neg Z) \\land X$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, we can factor out the conjunction with $X,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(X \\land Y) \\lor (X \\land \\neg Z) \\equiv X \\land (Y \\lor \\neg Z)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can write\n\\[\nX \\land (Y \\lor \\neg Z) \\equiv (Y \\lor \\neg Z) \\land X.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7078,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions"},"group":{"id":15103,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308789,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:16:51.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14796},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308799,"created":"2026-10-15T23