ibutive Laws"},"example":{"id":7078,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions"},"group":{"id":15103,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308822,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:17:30.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15494},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308831,"created":"2026-10-15T23:17:49.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14359,"number":14,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:17 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":86772,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7078,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(H \\land \\neg P) \\lor (K \\land \\neg P)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$\\neg P \\land (H \\lor K)$","choice2":"$ P \\land (\\neg H \\lor K)$","choice3":"$\\neg P \\lor (H \\land K)$","choice4":"$(H \\land K) \\land \\neg P $","choice5":"$\\neg P \\lor (H \\lor K)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, we can factor out the conjunction with $\\neg P,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(H \\land \\neg P) \\lor (K \\land \\neg P) \\equiv (H \\lor K) \\land \\neg P\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can write\n\\[\n(H \\lor K) \\land \\neg P \\equiv \\neg P \\land (H \\lor K).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7078,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions"},"group":{"id":15103,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308831,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:17:49.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14359},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308848,"created":"2026-10-15T23:18:09.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15109,"number":15,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:18 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":128645,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7078,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(A \\land C) \\lor (B \\land A)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(C \\lor B) \\land A$","choice2":"$C \\lor  (B \\land A)$","choice3":"$(C \\lor B)  \\lor A$","choice4":"$(C \\land B) \\land A$","choice5":"$C  \\land (B \\lor A)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First,  since $A \\lor C \\equiv C \\lor A,$ we can write\n\\[\n(A \\land C) \\lor (B \\land A) \\equiv (C \\land A) \\lor (B \\land A).\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then,  we can factor out the conjunction with $A,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(C \\land A) \\lor (B \\land A) \\equiv (C \\lor B) \\land A\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7078,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions"},"group":{"id":15103,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308848,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:18:09.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15109},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":7125,"number":4,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Disjunctions","answers":[{"id":62308862,"created":"2026-10-15T23:18:31.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15147,"number":16,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:18 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":81070,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7125,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(A \\lor B) \\land (A \\lor C)?$</p>\n","choice1":" $(B \\land C) \\lor A$","choice2":"  $(A \\land C) \\lor B$","choice3":"  $A \\land (B \\lor C)$","choice4":" $(A \\lor B) \\land C$","choice5":" $B \\lor (A \\land C)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, we can factor out the disjunction with $A,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(A \\lor B) \\land (A \\lor C) \\equiv A \\lor (B \\land C)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can write</p>\n<p>\\[\nA \\lor (B \\land C) \\equiv (B \\land C) \\lor A.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7125,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Disjunctions"},"group":{"id":15105,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308862,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:18:31.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15147},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308878,"created":"2026-10-15T23:18:52.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":17156,"number":17,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:18 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:17","question":{"id":86776,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7125,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(G \\lor H) \\land (\\neg K \\lor H)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$H \\lor (G \\land \\neg K)$","choice2":"$(G \\lor \\neg K) \\lor H $","choice3":"$H \\land (G \\lor \\neg K)$","choice4":"$\\neg H \\land (G \\lor K)$","choice5":"$(G \\land \\neg K) \\land H $","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, we can factor out the disjunction with $H,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(G \\lor H) \\land (\\neg K \\lor H) \\equiv (G \\land \\neg K) \\lor H\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can write</p>\n<p>\\[\n(G \\land \\neg K) \\lor H \\equiv H \\lor (G \\land \\neg K).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7125,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Disjunctions"},"group":{"id":15105,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308878,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:18:52.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":17156},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308899,"created":"2026-10-15T23:19:11.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15562,"number":18,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:19 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":128650,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7125,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(\\neg X \\lor \\neg Z) \\land (\\neg Y \\lor \\neg Z)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(\\neg X \\land \\neg Y) \\lor \\neg Z$","choice2":"$(\\neg X \\land \\neg Z) \\lor \\neg Y$","choice3":"$(\\neg X \\lor \\neg Y) \\land \\neg Z$","choice4":"$\\neg Z \\land (\\neg X \\land \\neg Y) $","choice5":"$\\neg Z \\lor (\\neg X \\lor \\neg Y) $","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We can factor out the disjunction with $\\neg Z,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(\\neg X \\lor \\neg Z) \\land (\\neg Y \\lor \\neg Z) \\equiv (\\neg X \\land \\neg Y) \\lor \\neg Z\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7125,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Disjunctions"},"group":{"id":15105,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308899,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:19:11.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15562},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308908,"created":"2026-10-15T23:19:29.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13371,"number":19,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:19 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":81621,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7125,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(\\neg P \\lor R) \\land (\\neg P \\lor Q)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(R \\land Q) \\lor \\neg P$","choice2":"$P \\lor (R \\land Q)$","choice3":"$(R \\land Q) \\land \\neg P$","choice4":"$P \\lor (\\neg R \\land Q)$","choice5":"$\\neg P  \\lor (R \\lor Q) $","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, we can factor out the disjunction with $\\neg P,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(\\neg P \\lor R) \\land (\\neg P \\lor Q) \\equiv \\neg P \\lor (R \\land Q)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can write</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\neg P \\lor (R \\land Q) \\equiv (R \\land Q) \\lor \\neg P.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7125,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Disjunctions"},"group":{"id":15105,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251681,"answer":{"id":62308908,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:19:29.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13371},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308918,"created":"2026-10-15T23:19:46.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13469,"number":20,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:19 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":128651,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7125,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(\\neg P \\lor Q) \\land (\\neg P \\lor \\neg R)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$\\neg P \\lor (Q \\land \\neg R)$","choice2":"$P \\lor (\\neg Q \\land \\neg \\neg R)$","choice3":"$\\neg P \\land (Q \\lor \\neg R)$","choice4":"$\\neg P \\lor (Q \\lor \\neg R)$","choice5":"$\\neg P \\land (Q \\land \\neg R)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We can factor out the disjunction with $\\neg P,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(\\neg P \\lor Q) \\land (\\neg P \\lor \\neg R) \\equiv \\neg P \\lor (Q \\land \\neg R)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":28